Hi <%= @user.display_login %>,

Your <%= Copilot.individual_product_name %> plan expires in one week and won't renew automatically.

When it does, your account will transition to Copilot Free. You'll still have access to Copilot at no cost, but your paid plan benefits — including model choices and higher usage — will end.

You still have time to switch

If you'd like uninterrupted access to the full Copilot experience, switch to a monthly Copilot Pro or Pro+ plan before your annual plan expires. You'll receive prorated credits for the remaining value of your annual subscription that can be used throughout the lifetime of your Copilot subscription.

- Copilot Pro: $<%= Copilot::COPILOT_PRO_MONTHLY_BASE_PRICE %>/month (see pricing page at https://github.com/features/copilot/plans for more plan details and current pricing)
- Copilot Pro+: $<%= Copilot::COPILOT_PRO_PLUS_MONTHLY_BASE_PRICE %>/month (see pricing page at https://github.com/features/copilot/plans for more plan details and current pricing)

Next steps

- Switch to monthly or manage your plan: <%= @settings_user_billing_path %>
- Learn more about plan options: <%= Copilot::COPILOT_FOR_INDIVIDUALS_BILLING_DOCUMENTATION %>
- Read the billing documentation: <%= Copilot::COPILOT_BILLING_DOCUMENTATION %>
- Read the blog post & FAQ: GitHub Copilot is moving to usage-based billing: https://github.blog/news-insights/company-news/github-copilot-is-moving-to-usage-based-billing/

We appreciate you being part of the Copilot community.

